course: dictionary
lesson: 8069
title: Reliable: can you trust it?
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Reliable means you can trust someone or something to do what is expected, every time. A reliable friend turns up when they said they would. A reliable car starts on a cold morning.
explain: In science, a test is reliable when you repeat it and get the same results again. «Measuring the same thing several times and taking the average gives a more reliable result.» Adding up the results and dividing by how many there are gives an answer you can trust more.
explain: Information is reliable when it is likely to be true and correct. Before you believe something, ask who wrote it and how they know. A reliable source checks its facts carefully.
fact: Reliable means you can trust someone or something to do what is expected, every time.
fact: Reliable information is likely to be true and correct.
fact: The opposite of reliable is unreliable, which means you cannot count on it.
fact: In a science test, a reliable result comes back the same each time you repeat the test.
fact: Reliable is an adjective, so it has forms: reliable, more reliable, most reliable.
exercise: «Measuring the same thing several times and taking the average gives a more reliable result.» What does reliable mean here? | *A result you can trust because it is likely to be correct | A result that is very big | A result that is found only once | A result that is written in pencil
exercise: «He has been a reliable friend for years.» What does reliable mean? | He is always late | *You can trust him to do what is expected | He is very loud | He has lots of money
exercise: Which is the most reliable source for facts about the Romans? | A guess from a game | A rumour from a friend of a friend | A post with no name on it | *A book by historians who check their facts
test: «A dog's nose temperature changes through the day, so a warm, dry nose is not a reliable sign of illness.» What does reliable sign mean? | A sign that a dog is happy | A sign that is hard to see | A sign that is always warm | *A sign you can trust to show what is really wrong
test: What is the opposite of reliable? | Honest | Clear | *Unreliable | Trustworthy
exam: Mia repeats her science test three times and gets the same result each time. What does this show? | *Her test is reliable | Her test is too short | Her test is finished | Her test is unfair
